From 9d6581add95310bd3a43d0ec0c68f3fac4466f72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AzediZ <145237384+AzediZ@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:39:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 55/63] Bills: due dates skip the time the server was off

Bills, office rent, alliance and sov billing and war bills run on real time. On a server that is
only on while it's being played, a week away could make an alliance bill overdue (closing the
alliance and dropping its sov), drop sov claims and impound offices, without anyone having been
able to pay.

- The server saves a heartbeat (srvStatus.lastHeartbeat, new migration) every minute and at
  shutdown.
- At start, before anything loads them, unpaid bill due dates, office lease expiry, alliance and sov
  next-bill dates and war next-bill dates move on by the time since the last heartbeat (when that
  is over 5 minutes). The log says how long the server was off.
- New setting <corp><PauseBillsWhileOff> (default true). false = due dates run on real time, as
  before.
